        <body>
            <div xml:id="d159">

                <pb facs="0413" n="317" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg317"/>

                <head>No. 157.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Henderson to Mr. Davis.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Consulate</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Amoy</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1874-06-06"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">June</hi> 6, 1874</date>. (Received August
                        5.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 32.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose copies of
                    correspondence between Com. A. Kautz, U. S. N., and myself, on the subject of
                    the Japanese expedition to Formosa and American intervention therein. Also copy
                    of a notification which I have issued in co-operation with the United States
                    naval forces on this station, hoping it will, in view of the peculiarity of
                    attending circumstances, meet the approval of the Government, and may be, for
                    the time being, discourage Americans from having anything more to do with that
                    enterprise.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>J. J. HENDERSON.</signed></closer>





